Found 2026-09-27 while wiring karr-doc-writer in ../karr: briefing.skills entry `mattpocock-skills:domain-modeling` -> spawn denied ("references unknown skill(s)"), although the skill is installed and loads fine via the Skill tool.

Claude Code caches plugins as ~/.claude/plugins/cache/<marketplace>/<plugin>/<version>/skills/..., e.g.
  ~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/mattpocock-skills/1.2.3/skills/engineering/domain-modeling/SKILL.md

resolve_skill (hooks/briefing-preload:174) only globs
  cache/<plugin>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md
  cache/*/<plugin>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md        (:183)
and for bare names cache/*/skills/<name> and cache/*/*/skills/<name> (:196) -- no <version> segment in any of them. The Codex resolver (:459ff) already knows about the versioned path.

Second gap: some plugins nest skills one level deeper by category (mattpocock-skills: skills/{engineering,productivity,misc,...}/<skill>/), which neither pattern reaches.

Expected: plugin:skill resolves the way Claude Code itself resolves it -- versioned cache dir (pick the installed/highest version), and a skill dir found anywhere under the plugin's skills/ tree. Add a test with a fake versioned + category-nested cache.
